# Mutation plan for the user family on the local socket (`crates/mm-api/src/local_users.rs`,
# the port of `api4/user_local.go`).
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/local-users.plan
#
# The seventeen wrapped HTTP handlers are mutated by their own plans. What this file tests is
# what the local family adds: the `local*` functions that are the HTTP handler *minus* a check
# (the permission gates of `getUsers`, the self check of `getUploadsForUser`, the restrictions
# of the single-user reads), the session each wrapper hands its handler, and the transport a
# shared handler's forward branch takes when the request came in on the socket.
#
# `proxy-forwards-a-socket-request-over-the-port` is the line worth reading twice. Every shared
# handler forwards through `proxy::forward_to_go`, which since this family checks for the
# `GoLocalSocket` request extension and dials the socket. Without that check the MFA
# deactivation — the one forward `the_local_auth_token_and_conversion_routes_match_over_the_socket`
# reaches — goes over the port to `APISessionRequiredMfa`, which is a 401 for a request Go's
# local handler answers 200.
#
# Not planned, because equivalent: moving the role-parameter forward after the local 400s.
# `?role=…&not_in_channel=…` is a `team_id` 400 either way — served here, or forwarded to a Go
# that validates the role first and then refuses the same thing — and the suite has no way to
# tell those apart that it should want.
